// Base game plants: a shared pool biomes draw from by tag or name. Each names its block (a
// plant's other looks, its variants such as pairs and clumps, are chosen by position), and
// says where it grows: the ground (Soil, Snow, Sand), its habitat (Anywhere, Open, Shade,
// Understory: thickest in shade, Water, Shore), the climate it is comfortable in, and how
// it spreads: Cover carpets the ground (grasses, ferns), Drifts grow in patches of one kind
// (flowers, herbs; kept sparse), Alone here and there (bushes, fungi, reeds; a biome's weight
// for these is their chance in a hundred per block). `snowy` names its look under snow. A
// plant's tags are its block's plus its own, and its properties (nutrition, alchemy, dye)
// default to what the block's tags say.
(
    plants: [
        // Grasses and ferns.
        (name: "short_grass", block: "short_grass", habitat: Open),
        (name: "tall_grass", block: "tall_grass", top: "tall_grass_top", habitat: Open, comfort: (moisture: (0.75, 8.0))),
        (name: "fern", block: "fern", habitat: Understory, comfort: (moisture: (0.8, 8.0))),
        (name: "large_fern", block: "large_fern", top: "large_fern_top", habitat: Shade, comfort: (moisture: (0.9, 8.0))),

